%U A400230 0,0,2,0,2,1,0,2,0,1,2,0,1,0,1,2,4,0,0
%N A400230 The sequence of y-values that occur when drawing a sequence of squares in the plane with integer side lengths such that the bottom-left corner of the k-th square is at the nonnegative integer point (k, a(k)) and the square has side length s_k, subject to the conditions that (1) the interior of each square has a distinct pattern made by the perimeters of the other squares, and (2) the sequence (s_0, a(0), s_1, a(1), s_2, a(2), ...) is the lexicographically earliest such infinite sequence.
%H A400230 Peter Kagey, <a href="https://codegolf.stackexchange.com/q/291882/53884">The Eternal Internal Patterns of Squares</a>, Code Golf Stack Exchange.
%e A400230 The sequence of squares where the first square has side length A400229(0)=1, and y-value a(0)=0; the next has side length A400229(1)=2 and y-value a(1)=0; and so on. The index of each square is marked in the lower right corner, where A=10, B=11, and C=12.
